explanation:
`CatCommSq T L R B` holds an isomorphism `T ⋙ R ≅ L ⋙ B`. The body builds the composite isomorphism through these steps:

1. H₁⋙(R₁⋙R₂) ≅ (H₁⋙R₁)⋙R₂, by the inverse associator;
2. ≅ (L₁⋙H₂)⋙R₂, by the first square whiskered on the right by R₂;
3. ≅ L₁⋙(H₂⋙R₂), by the associator;
4. ≅ L₁⋙(L₂⋙H₃), by the second square whiskered on the left by L₁;
5. ≅ (L₁⋙L₂)⋙H₃, by the inverse associator.

This is exactly the standard pasting of two 2-cells along their shared edge H₂, and every type matches the intended square. The construction is the specific 2-categorical operation for squares in Cat, which is what this file is about. Mathlib has no separate, more general version of this particular CatCommSq construction, so it is not too narrow.
